finding: The stage's full-cone-with-filter-margin claim fails near the wide boundary. src/standard/rendering/shadows.ts:930 adds 2*EDGE_TEXELS/tilePx to tan(outer), but the actual cone-edge inset in tile pixels is tilePx/2*(1-tan(outer)/coneTanHalf). Independent evaluation at tilePx=512 gives only 0.527890 px at 80 degrees, 0.262197 px at 85 degrees, and 0.052354 px at 89 degrees, not the three-texel filter margin. Even Hardware2x2's half-texel footprint does not fit at 85/89 degrees; the Gaussian taps extend farther. shade.ts clamps these taps to the tile instead of sampling a fully rendered footprint. The new projection tests only require ndc <= 1 (plus epsilon), and the ordinary-margin test enshrines the additive expression; neither proves filter containment, so both pass despite this failure. Prove the supported wide cone plus its actual filter footprint fits without moving the required ordinary controls.
